Subject: Import a ColorBuffer's Metal heap without a dedicated image on MoltenVK

On macOS the renderer imports the Metal heap of a ColorBuffer into the memory of every buffer a
guest process makes an image of. The guest driver passes no dedicated allocation to the host
when it picks a host-visible memory type, which is the type it picks on Apple silicon, so the
renderer made one up: a dedicated allocation of the ColorBuffer's own image. MoltenVK then
refused to bind the guest's image to that memory ("Could not bind VkImage to a VkDeviceMemory
dedicated to resource ... A dedicated allocation may only be used with the resource it was
dedicated to", VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_DEVICE_MEMORY). ANGLE turned the failed bind into
EGL_BAD_PARAMETER, so every buffer SurfaceFlinger imported failed with "Could not create EGL
image, err = (0x300c)" and every app window stayed black.

An import that names no image is now made without a dedicated allocation. An import that names
the guest's image keeps it.

Applies after 0042 on gfxstream d047a57228332d995d36600792fa9ccc26cf8ae6.
---
diff --git a/host/vulkan/VkDecoderGlobalState.cpp b/host/vulkan/VkDecoderGlobalState.cpp
--- a/host/vulkan/VkDecoderGlobalState.cpp
+++ b/host/vulkan/VkDecoderGlobalState.cpp
@@ -5359,18 +5359,16 @@
                 // Use metal object extension on MoltenVK mode for color buffer import,
                 // non-moltenVK path on MacOS will use FD handles
                 if (m_vkEmulation->supportsMoltenVk()) {
-                    if (dedicatedAllocInfoPtr == nullptr || localDedicatedAllocInfo.image == VK_NULL_HANDLE) {
-                        // TODO(b/351765838): This should not happen, but somehow the guest
-                        // is not providing us the necessary information for video rendering.
-                        localDedicatedAllocInfo = {
-                            .sType = VK_STRUCTURE_TYPE_MEMORY_DEDICATED_ALLOCATE_INFO,
-                            .pNext = nullptr,
-                            .image =
-                                m_vkEmulation->getColorBufferVkImage(importCbInfoPtr->colorBuffer),
-                            .buffer = VK_NULL_HANDLE,
-                        };
-
-                        shouldUseDedicatedAllocInfo = true;
+                    if (dedicatedAllocInfoPtr == nullptr ||
+                        localDedicatedAllocInfo.image == VK_NULL_HANDLE) {
+                        // The guest names no image when it allocates the memory of a host-visible
+                        // type, so the import has none to be dedicated to. It was dedicated to
+                        // the ColorBuffer's own image, and then MoltenVK refused to bind the
+                        // guest's image to it ("A dedicated allocation may only be used with the
+                        // resource it was dedicated to"), which failed every import of a buffer
+                        // the guest made an image of. The heap is imported without a dedicated
+                        // image, and any image of the right size binds to it.
+                        shouldUseDedicatedAllocInfo = false;
                     }
 
                     MTLResource_id cbExtMemoryHandle =
